# Frontend standards (Clean Architecture)

JS/TS UI is **TypeScript only**. Do **not** reshuffle existing `pages/`, `components/`, `hooks/` unless the user asks.

## Architecture — Clean Architecture (inward only)

Apply to **new** modules under `resources/ts/`:

```
Presentation → Application → Domain
Infrastructure → Domain
```

```text
resources/ts/domain/           # entities, ports — no React, no fetch
resources/ts/application/      # use cases — orchestrate ports only
resources/ts/infrastructure/   # HTTP, storage, env, DI
resources/ts/presentation/     # views, stores, providers
```

- Depend inward. Infrastructure implements domain ports.
- Wire in a composition root (`resources/ts/infrastructure/di/container.ts`).
- Pages only gate + compose features — no fetch/SSE/business state.
- Split UI: shell / list / item / composer / view. Avoid god components (~200 lines/file).

Existing Inertia pages live in `resources/ts/pages/` — keep using them; put new domain logic in the layers above, not inside the page file.

## TypeScript (strict)

- `"strict": true` — do not disable. Prefer `allowJs: false`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`.
- **No `any`**. JSON boundary: `unknown` → parse to typed entities.
- Explicit return types on exported functions, hooks, and use-case `execute`.
- No non-null `!` unless proven. Handle `T | undefined` from index access.

```ts
// ❌ const id = (data as any).id;
// ✅ parse unknown → string / entity; throw on invalid shape
```

## Lint / format

- Fix ESLint violations; do not disable rules without reason.
- Follow this repo’s formatter/config; do not add a new formatter stack unless asked.

## Forbidden

- Business logic or `fetch` / SSE parse inside components
- `any`, `as any`, or disabling strict checks
- Domain importing React or HTTP clients
- Migrating old folders “to match the rule” without an explicit request
